Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.05,0:00:25.01,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.09,0:00:27.73,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.81,0:00:28.77,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.85,0:00:29.89,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.01,0:00:31.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Your moves!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.63,0:01:07.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Now listen to me, Rebecca.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.29,0:01:09.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm only going to say this one more time.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.37,0:01:12.29,Default,,0,0,0,,My grandpa didn't steal\Nyour blue-eyes white dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.37,0:01:13.20,Default,,0,0,0,,You're lying!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.59,0:01:20.36,Default,,0,0,0,,It was my grandpa's favorite, and\Nyour grandpa took it from him.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.35,0:01:24.11,Default,,0,0,0,,You won't get away with this, you thieves!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.55,0:01:26.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Rebecca.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.77,0:01:27.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Now what?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.68,0:01:30.35,Default,,0,0,0,,There's a story that you\Nneed to hear, Rebecca.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.79,0:01:33.33,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the story of how\NI met your grandfather,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.41,0:01:36.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Professor Arthur Hawkins, and\Nof the danger we face together.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.93,0:01:40.13,Default,,0,0,0,,In other words, more of\Nyour lies. Forget it!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.35,0:01:41.33,Default,,0,0,0,,No, it's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.55,0:01:42.38,Default,,0,0,0,,And be assured,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.46,0:01:46.20,Default,,0,0,0,,it was one of the most frightening\Nexperiences I've had in my entire life.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.29,0:01:47.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm, I'm so sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.79,0:01:49.39,Default,,0,0,0,,It happened years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.25,0:01:52.73,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's an adventure I'll never forget.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.59,0:01:58.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I had traveled to Egypt to\Nparticipate in an archaeological dig.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.05,0:02:03.05,Default,,0,0,0,,A brand new discovery had been made\Nnot far from the Great Pyramids.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.19,0:02:08.45,Default,,0,0,0,,We all wondered what ancient Egyptian\Nsecrets would soon be unearthed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.55,0:02:12.75,Default,,0,0,0,,The desert was hotter and\Ndrier than I expected.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.53,0:02:17.45,Default,,0,0,0,,So it was fortunate that\NI soon made a friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.95,0:02:20.54,Default,,0,0,0,,You look like you could\Nuse some cool water.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.87,0:02:22.17,Default,,0,0,0,,How can I thank you?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.73,0:02:25.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I guzzled it down a little too quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.67,0:02:32.26,Default,,0,0,0,,But my new friend, Professor Arthur\NHawkins, was just amused at my enthusiasm.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.67,0:02:34.93,Default,,0,0,0,,He was a kind and very brilliant man.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.33,0:02:40.01,Default,,0,0,0,,But in his field of archaeology, he was\Nviewed as an extremely radical thinker.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.33,0:02:41.16,Default,,0,0,0,,How come?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.75,0:02:42.79,Default,,0,0,0,,His theories.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.13,0:02:45.29,Default,,0,0,0,,He believed that dual\Nmonsters may have played
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.37,0:02:47.78,Default,,0,0,0,,some mysterious part in Egyptian history.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.99,0:02:49.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Am I right, Rebecca?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.73,0:02:52.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't understand, Grandpa.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.67,0:02:56.27,Default,,0,0,0,,His study of hieroglyphics,\Nthe ancient Egyptians'
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.35,0:03:00.17,Default,,0,0,0,,writing, kept turning up one\Nparticular word over and over again.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.25,0:03:02.63,Default,,0,0,0,,And that one word was "dual.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.63,0:03:05.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh? Dual?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.39,0:03:06.39,Default,,0,0,0,,But why?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.17,0:03:08.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.11,0:03:11.31,Default,,0,0,0,,It was a mystery.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.59,0:03:18.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Using dual as a key word, he worked toward\Na new interpretation of Egyptian history.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.57,0:03:21.98,Default,,0,0,0,,And he came to an astonishing conclusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.11,0:03:24.29,Default,,0,0,0,,It's here, my friend,\Nin these hieroglyphs.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.37,0:03:26.19,Default,,0,0,0,,By the spirits of the River Nile,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.27,0:03:30.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I combine magic and monster to vanquish\Nmy enemy in our battle this day.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.97,0:03:32.77,Default,,0,0,0,,What on earth can that mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.09,0:03:34.43,Default,,0,0,0,,If I'm correct,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.71,0:03:39.67,Default,,0,0,0,,it has to do with incredible contests\Nin which ancient Egyptians participated.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.61,0:03:42.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Contests with high stakes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.45,0:03:44.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I believe duels.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.41,0:03:45.75,Default,,0,0,0,,What kind of duels?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.93,0:03:49.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I think you'll find the answer\Nin that inscription, Solomon.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.41,0:03:51.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at this.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.43,0:03:53.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Duel monsters cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.73,0:03:59.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Now take a look at those ancient drawings.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.49,0:04:01.71,Default,,0,0,0,,The images are nearly the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.93,0:04:04.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Which leads me to believe\Nthe ancient Egyptians
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.13,0:04:06.35,Default,,0,0,0,,must have played a\Nsimilar game to our own.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.43,0:04:07.79,Default,,0,0,0,,What an amazing discovery.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.87,0:04:10.35,Default,,0,0,0,,When you present it to\Nyour fellow scholars,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.43,0:04:13.35,Default,,0,0,0,,you'll revolutionize\Nthe field of Egyptology.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.05,0:04:15.13,Default,,0,0,0,,We shall see.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.45,0:04:16.63,Default,,0,0,0,,That's ridiculous.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.71,0:04:21.53,Default,,0,0,0,,But Arthur's colleagues ridiculed his\Ntheories and dismissed them as wild fantasy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.15,0:04:24.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Even in the face of such disbelief,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.39,0:04:27.13,Default,,0,0,0,,he bravely stood his ground\Nand continued his difficult
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.21,0:04:30.03,Default,,0,0,0,,research into the ancient\Ngame of duel monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.23,0:04:34.23,Default,,0,0,0,,He invited me to join him in his\Nwork, and I helped as best I could.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.45,0:04:38.49,Default,,0,0,0,,In time, he discovered a link between\Nthe game and the Millennium Items.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.57,0:04:39.85,Default,,0,0,0,,What kind of link?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.83,0:04:43.35,Default,,0,0,0,,It's still very mysterious, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.23,0:04:48.59,Default,,0,0,0,,The ancient Egyptians didn't play this\Ngame just for fun or money, Solomon,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.67,0:04:51.20,Default,,0,0,0,,but rather for the\Npower to rule the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.29,0:04:52.45,Default,,0,0,0,,How can that be?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.77,0:04:56.12,Default,,0,0,0,,The inscriptions tell of a\Nplace called the Shadow Realm,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.21,0:04:58.73,Default,,0,0,0,,where terrible monsters dwell and powerful
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.81,0:05:01.40,Default,,0,0,0,,warriors battle for\Ndominion over the earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.81,0:05:02.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.72,0:05:07.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Apparently, the ancient Egyptians actually\Nplayed the game in that mysterious realm.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.19,0:05:11.54,Default,,0,0,0,,And the stakes, according to this\Ninscription, were the fate of the earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.57,0:05:16.29,Default,,0,0,0,,So the stories I heard are\Ntrue, and your friend, Professor
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.37,0:05:18.87,Default,,0,0,0,,hawkins is that where your\Nblue eyes came from he
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.95,0:05:23.11,Default,,0,0,0,,gave it to you that's right\Nliar you were never his
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.19,0:05:26.25,Default,,0,0,0,,friend my grandpa would never\Nhave given away his blue eyes
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.33,0:05:30.31,Default,,0,0,0,,white dragon you stole it\Ni know you did isn't that
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.39,0:05:34.41,Default,,0,0,0,,right teddy no rebecca i\Ndidn't i couldn't have because
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.49,0:05:37.73,Default,,0,0,0,,at that precise moment that\Nancient tomb caved in around
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.81,0:05:43.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Us, huh? The tomb, he did. Yes,\Nand we thought we were lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.63,0:05:59.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Solomon over here Arthur are you\Nall right I think so but the cave-in
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.27,0:06:05.11,Default,,0,0,0,,has trapped us in this tomb there's\Nno way out wait I found the lamp as
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.19,0:06:10.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Time passed. We feared the Pharaoh's\Ngrave would become ours as well. We
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.49,0:06:15.71,Default,,0,0,0,,consumed what little food we had with\Nus soon nothing was left but a canteen
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.79,0:06:22.05,Default,,0,0,0,,of water enough for only one person\NSolomon yes Arthur what would you
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.13,0:06:26.71,Default,,0,0,0,,say to a duel now it'll help keep our\Nspirits up and give us something to
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.79,0:06:30.31,Default,,0,0,0,,think about besides our being trapped\Nit's better than sitting quietly
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.39,0:06:32.03,Default,,0,0,0,,in the dark waiting for the end to
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.11,0:06:37.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Come a hmm point taken, Arthur, I have
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.97,0:06:39.51,Default,,0,0,0,,an idea. I'm listening.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.87,0:06:42.71,Default,,0,0,0,,We have only a small amount of water left.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.79,0:06:45.93,Default,,0,0,0,,There's not enough for two\Npeople, so if we try to share it,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.01,0:06:49.07,Default,,0,0,0,,the chances are that neither of us\Nwill walk out of this tomb alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.15,0:06:53.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I propose that the last of the water\Nshould go to the winner of this duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.11,0:06:55.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you agree?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.02,0:06:56.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Sadly, I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.93,0:06:58.82,Default,,0,0,0,,And so our grim duel began.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.15,0:07:03.92,Default,,0,0,0,,In his first turn, the card that Arthur\Nplayed was the Witch of the Black Forest.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.75,0:07:06.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Sound familiar, Rebecca?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.61,0:07:09.39,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the same card she played.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.59,0:07:10.71,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.99,0:07:14.40,Default,,0,0,0,,It was your grandfather who\Ntaught you to duel, wasn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.49,0:07:16.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Never mind her.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.57,0:07:17.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Go on with the story.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.48,0:07:18.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, you see...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.67,0:07:19.97,Default,,0,0,0,,No more lies!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.29,0:07:21.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Why should I believe you?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.67,0:07:24.75,Default,,0,0,0,,You could be making this\Nwhole stupid story up! Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.93,0:07:26.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Moto doesn't lie.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.19,0:07:29.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, well, I think we\Nshould finish this duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.63,0:07:30.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.54,0:07:33.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, some of us would rather\Nhear the rest of the story first.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.09,0:07:34.62,Default,,0,0,0,,No, let the duel continue.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.59,0:07:40.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm, I think it's Yugi's turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.85,0:07:41.77,Default,,0,0,0,,We know that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.03,0:07:44.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Why don't you butt out, old man,\Nso we can settle this thing?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.05,0:07:46.87,Default,,0,0,0,,As you wish. Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.03,0:07:49.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll get back to kicking Yugi's butt.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.11,0:07:50.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, one thing's for certain.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.73,0:07:51.56,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.64,0:07:53.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Rebecca may have learned\Ndueling from Arthur,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.73,0:07:56.02,Default,,0,0,0,,but she never learned manners from him.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.43,0:07:59.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe this will teach her some.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.63,0:08:02.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I play Catapult Turtle in attack mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.01,0:08:07.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Catapult Turtle lets me sacrifice\Nany monster on my field. When I do,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.43,0:08:11.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I am then able to deduct half\Nof my sacrificed monster's
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.11,0:08:14.23,Default,,0,0,0,,attack power directly from\Nmy opponent's life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.53,0:08:16.57,Default,,0,0,0,,What a joke. That won't help.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.89,0:08:20.61,Default,,0,0,0,,It will when I combine it\Nwith my brain control. Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.47,0:08:26.71,Default,,0,0,0,,With brain control, I can seize any\Nmonster and control it for one turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.39,0:08:29.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Millennium Shield comes to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.49,0:08:37.63,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, I use Catapult Turtle to\Nsacrifice your Millennium Shield!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.31,0:08:42.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.33,0:08:45.45,Default,,0,0,0,,And my turn isn't over yet, Rebecca!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.13,0:08:48.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Summon Skull Attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.13,0:08:54.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Your cannon soldier is toast!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.49,0:08:57.81,Default,,0,0,0,,That's not fair!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.09,0:08:59.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm still gonna beat you, Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.83,0:09:02.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna get you and\Nyour thieving grandfather!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.01,0:09:13.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh, guess Yugi's a little\Nbetter duelist than I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.45,0:09:16.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Guess I can see how he won the\Nduelist kingdom tournament.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.19,0:09:18.81,Default,,0,0,0,,But he's never been up\Nagainst a genius before.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.89,0:09:22.77,Default,,0,0,0,,And everything is going\Naccording to plan. Let's see.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.05,0:09:26.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Right now I have six crummy\Nmonsters in my graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.81,0:09:28.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Not quite enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.57,0:09:36.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Great! Fantastic!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.11,0:09:37.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Look what card we drew, Teddy!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.83,0:09:40.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Bravo, bravo, Rebecca! What's so fun?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.57,0:09:43.37,Default,,0,0,0,,T for victory!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.19,0:09:48.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I play this magic card,\NJudgment Blaster! What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.39,0:09:53.49,Default,,0,0,0,,With Judgment Blaster, I can discard five\Ncards from my hands and in exchange...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.25,0:10:04.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I get to obliterate every\Nmonster you've got on the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.57,0:10:09.07,Default,,0,0,0,,And one more thing, now I\Nsummon my favorite monster!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.97,0:10:17.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Up from the depths comes the creepy and\Noh-so-lovable Shadow Ghoul in attack mode!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.25,0:10:20.83,Default,,0,0,0,,And for each of the lame-o\Nmonsters in my graveyard,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.91,0:10:24.03,Default,,0,0,0,,this adorable fella gains\Nan extra 100 attack points!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.99,0:10:26.29,Default,,0,0,0,,For each monster?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.49,0:10:27.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I lost count, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.93,0:10:29.83,Default,,0,0,0,,How many monsters has she\Nsent to the graveyard?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.91,0:10:31.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I think it's 11.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.23,0:10:35.93,Default,,0,0,0,,100, 200, 3... 1,100. Uh-huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.19,0:10:38.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Shadow Ghoul now has an\Nattack power of 2,700.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.79,0:10:40.62,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.70,0:10:43.94,Default,,0,0,0,,You mean you sacrificed 11\Nmonsters to the graveyard just
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.03,0:10:46.73,Default,,0,0,0,,so you could use their energy\Nto power up your Shadow Ghoul?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.81,0:10:49.29,Default,,0,0,0,,You're just now catching\Non to my strategy, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.37,0:10:51.61,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll have to think faster than that.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.67,0:10:53.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Rebecca...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.58,0:10:54.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Now what?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.49,0:10:58.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Duel monsters isn't about tossing\Naside all your best creatures.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.17,0:11:01.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Each monster has its own abilities\Nand demands its own kind of respect.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.97,0:11:03.27,Default,,0,0,0,,If you just throw them away...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.35,0:11:04.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you out of your mind?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.01,0:11:09.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Dueling has nothing to do\Nwith respecting your monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.09,0:11:12.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Everyone knows the only thing\Nthat really matters is winning.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.55,0:11:16.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Besides, what would a family of thieves\Nknow about a duelist's real power?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.93,0:11:20.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I learned my dueling strategy\Nfrom a master, my grandfather.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.15,0:11:23.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Anyway, duel monsters aren't real.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.19,0:11:24.51,Default,,0,0,0,,They're just ink on cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.59,0:11:25.65,Default,,0,0,0,,What's to respect?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.85,0:11:27.67,Default,,0,0,0,,That's not what Arthur thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.55,0:11:31.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Rebecca understands the strategy\Nand tactics of duel monsters,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.97,0:11:34.62,Default,,0,0,0,,but she's never found\Nthe heart of the cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.77,0:11:39.30,Default,,0,0,0,,If anyone can teach Rebecca the lessons\Nshe needs to learn, it's my grandson.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.73,0:11:43.39,Default,,0,0,0,,You're keeping me waiting, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.47,0:11:45.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't come here to take a nap.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.09,0:11:46.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I came to duel!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.27,0:11:48.39,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.63,0:11:50.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I summon a monster in defense mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.35,0:11:57.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, well.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.71,0:12:00.89,Default,,0,0,0,,What you think I lack in\Nrespect, I make up in talent.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.31,0:12:03.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I drew a magic card. Stop defense.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.51,0:12:08.35,Default,,0,0,0,,She's forced the Dark\NMagician into attack mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.43,0:12:11.29,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, Shadow Ghoul attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.59,0:12:12.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Green Paper Shroud!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.97,0:12:22.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Bye-bye, Dark Magician.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.13,0:12:24.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.04,0:12:26.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Moto, Yugi's getting creamed.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.63,0:12:29.63,Default,,0,0,0,,This couldn't be how your duel\Nwith Professor Hawkins went.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.71,0:12:32.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Actually, it went exactly like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.65,0:12:35.67,Default,,0,0,0,,But the outcome of this\Nduel may yet surprise you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.19,0:12:38.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I play Swords of Revealing Life.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.93,0:12:42.40,Default,,0,0,0,,That will keep you from attacking\Nfor three turns, Rebecca.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.69,0:12:44.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, that's really irritating.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.55,0:12:45.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.79,0:12:48.49,Default,,0,0,0,,If that's the case, I\Npass this turn. Yeesh.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.69,0:12:50.10,Default,,0,0,0,,It didn't even faze her.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.29,0:12:52.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I can use this card.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.89,0:12:53.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Monster Reborn!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.57,0:12:56.87,Default,,0,0,0,,To resurrect the Dark Magician!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.21,0:12:59.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.12,0:13:03.30,Default,,0,0,0,,He's trying to reassemble his forces, Teddy,\Nwhile I'm prevented from attacking him.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.39,0:13:04.80,Default,,0,0,0,,But that won't save him.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.49,0:13:08.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll play my next card in defense\Nmode, and I'll tell him what it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.69,0:13:11.57,Default,,0,0,0,,because there's no way he\Ncan beat my genius brain.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.65,0:13:12.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Whee!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.56,0:13:13.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Another cannon soldier!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.23,0:13:16.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Smart move.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.33,0:13:20.27,Default,,0,0,0,,She wants me to attack, but I can't\Nlet that cannon soldier get off a shot.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.35,0:13:21.83,Default,,0,0,0,,You want an attack, Rebecca?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.91,0:13:23.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, here it comes!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.31,0:13:25.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Dark Magician, attack cannon soldier!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.87,0:13:31.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmph. Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.33,0:13:35.29,Default,,0,0,0,,You've just raised Shadow Ghoul's\Nattack power by another hundred points!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.37,0:13:39.65,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter what card Yugi draws next,\Nthat ghoul's more powerful than ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.73,0:13:41.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Rebecca's strategy seems to be working.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.99,0:13:43.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe she is a genius.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.51,0:13:45.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't count Yuge out yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.67,0:13:47.26,Default,,0,0,0,,He learned from the master.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.35,0:13:48.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, I understand now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.25,0:13:52.21,Default,,0,0,0,,You're using the Swords of\NRevealing Light to stall for time,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.29,0:13:54.23,Default,,0,0,0,,hoping for some special card to come up.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.31,0:13:57.39,Default,,0,0,0,,But that isn't going to help\Nhim at all, is it, Teddy?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.47,0:13:59.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Not one Shadow Ghoul can attack again!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.33,0:14:01.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll pass this turn, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.17,0:14:06.45,Default,,0,0,0,,But next time, when my Ghoul's\Nfree to attack, I'll wipe you out!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.55,0:14:09.61,Default,,0,0,0,,So, Solomon,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.91,0:14:15.13,Default,,0,0,0,,on my next turn I'll be free to attack,\NBut I'm going to pass this turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.35,0:14:17.73,Default,,0,0,0,,If that's really what you want to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.03,0:14:20.32,Default,,0,0,0,,What card are you waiting for, Solomon?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.61,0:14:21.93,Default,,0,0,0,,That's my secret.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.33,0:14:28.74,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the matter, Yugi?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.87,0:14:30.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Didn't you get the card you need?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.19,0:14:36.77,Default,,0,0,0,,So, Solomon, did you\Nget the card you need?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.61,0:14:44.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Come now, don't keep me in suspense.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.01,0:14:48.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I surrender, Arthur.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.23,0:14:50.25,Default,,0,0,0,,You win.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.15,0:14:58.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I surrender, Rebecca.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.43,0:15:02.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't believe it!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.43,0:15:03.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi's given up!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.15,0:15:11.87,Default,,0,0,0,,The game's over, Rebecca.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.69,0:15:14.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Unbelievable.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.07,0:15:18.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, why?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.37,0:15:20.08,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't just give up, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.55,0:15:24.97,Default,,0,0,0,,You mean I win?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.21,0:15:26.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, you win, Rebecca.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.69,0:15:28.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Bravo!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.60,0:15:29.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Yay, me!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.51,0:15:30.40,Default,,0,0,0,,We beat him, Teddy!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.57,0:15:32.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Rebecca the Genius wins!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.75,0:15:34.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.97,0:15:36.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Why did you surrender?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.25,0:15:38.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, what's up with that, Yugi?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.15,0:15:38.98,Default,,0,0,0,,I won!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.07,0:15:40.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Now give me the blue eyes!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.11,0:15:47.73,Default,,0,0,0,,You tore it! Oh no!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.93,0:15:50.35,Default,,0,0,0,,You destroyed my\Ngrandfather's favorite card!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.43,0:15:51.35,Default,,0,0,0,,It wasn't me, Rebecca.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.43,0:15:54.09,Default,,0,0,0,,First you steal it, then\Nyou lie, then you ruin it!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.17,0:15:55.99,Default,,0,0,0,,You despicable, mean man!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.17,0:15:57.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I treasured that card, Rebecca.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.15,0:15:59.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I would never have destroyed it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.03,0:16:02.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I've heard just about enough of your lies!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.25,0:16:03.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Rebecca, behave yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.81,0:16:07.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandpa? Arthur?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.61,0:16:09.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Arthur, is it really you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.99,0:16:11.89,Default,,0,0,0,,It's been a long time, Solomon.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.21,0:16:14.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Far too long, my dear old friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.83,0:16:18.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I do hope my precocious granddaughter\Nhasn't caused you too much trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.89,0:16:20.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you forgive her?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.63,0:16:21.55,Default,,0,0,0,,For what?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.93,0:16:26.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Rebecca, did you know Yugi was\Nactually the winner of your duel? No!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.29,0:16:27.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandpa, I won!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.23,0:16:30.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, you're just like your grandfather.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.31,0:16:33.53,Default,,0,0,0,,You're a generous young man,\Nand a very fine duelist.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.33,0:16:37.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.93,0:16:40.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Rebecca, have a look at this card. Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.25,0:16:43.17,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a card called Soul Release.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.61,0:16:46.17,Default,,0,0,0,,If Yugi had played this\Ncard in the final turn,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.25,0:16:48.35,Default,,0,0,0,,you would have been defeated for certain.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.43,0:16:52.87,Default,,0,0,0,,With Soul Release, Yugi could have freed\Nup to five cards from his graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.95,0:16:53.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Or yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.05,0:16:55.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you realize what that means?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.85,0:17:00.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Shadow Ghoul's attack power would\Nhave instantly dropped from 2800 to 2300.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.25,0:17:05.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi's Dark Magician had an attack\Npower of 2500, and therefore...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.43,0:17:10.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh, you mean Yugi really\Nnever had to surrender?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.91,0:17:11.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Then why?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.79,0:17:14.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.31,0:17:16.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi wanted to show you that there's much
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.43,0:17:18.69,Default,,0,0,0,,more to dueling than\Njust winning and losing.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.77,0:17:20.61,Default,,0,0,0,,He wanted you to see that the way to the
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.69,0:17:23.34,Default,,0,0,0,,heart of the cards is\Nthrough your own heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.43,0:17:27.71,Default,,0,0,0,,After that tomb collapsed and\Nwe'd bet our last drop of water
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.79,0:17:32.01,Default,,0,0,0,,On the duel, Solomon also sacrificed\Na victory to save my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.91,0:17:36.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I felt weak, overcome by the heat
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.53,0:17:40.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on, my friend
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.99,0:17:45.99,Default,,0,0,0,,You didn't have to surrender I\Ncouldn't let you lose this duel,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.11,0:17:49.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Arthur You need the\Nwater Solomon, thank you
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.59,0:17:57.81,Default,,0,0,0,,We did it!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.99,0:17:59.23,Default,,0,0,0,,We've broken through!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.47,0:18:00.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you down there?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.41,0:18:02.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you survive?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.25,0:18:06.39,Default,,0,0,0,,He saved my life, Rebecca.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.91,0:18:08.15,Default,,0,0,0,,But there's more.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.45,0:18:10.07,Default,,0,0,0,,In my duel with Solomon,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.37,0:18:13.09,Default,,0,0,0,,it's true that I sent any\Nnumber of monsters to the
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.17,0:18:16.58,Default,,0,0,0,,graveyard to bring the Shadow\NGhoul to its ultimate power.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.17,0:18:21.21,Default,,0,0,0,,But I never failed to honor those\Nmonsters for their sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.29,0:18:23.12,Default,,0,0,0,,In their own way,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.20,0:18:27.30,Default,,0,0,0,,they were every bit as important to\Nme as the Shadow Ghoul card itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.41,0:18:33.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Even more than the monsters, though, a\Nduelist must always respect his opponent.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.47,0:18:34.55,Default,,0,0,0,,In Solomon's case,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.75,0:18:39.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I felt such respect and gratitude that\NI gave him my Blue-Eyes White Dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.89,0:18:43.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and he showed his respect\Nand thanks by ripping it up!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.93,0:18:46.45,Default,,0,0,0,,It was damaged, Arthur. Forgive me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.85,0:18:48.39,Default,,0,0,0,,That doesn't matter, Solomon.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.47,0:18:51.61,Default,,0,0,0,,What matters is that you kept\Nit as a token of our friendship.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.69,0:18:55.67,Default,,0,0,0,,You valued the card not for its\Nrarity, but for what it represents,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.91,0:18:57.45,Default,,0,0,0,,the bond between us.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.85,0:18:59.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Now do you understand, Rebecca?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.75,0:19:02.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Great duels can form the\Nbasis of great and lasting
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.89,0:19:06.77,Default,,0,0,0,,friendships because the cards\Nare about heart. My heart?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.97,0:19:08.56,Default,,0,0,0,,The heart of every duelist.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.69,0:19:10.23,Default,,0,0,0,,And the heart of the cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.31,0:19:12.66,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what Yugi was trying to show you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.67,0:19:15.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Yugi, I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.03,0:19:17.21,Default,,0,0,0,,It's okay, Rebecca.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.11,0:19:20.41,Default,,0,0,0,,You mean you forgive me? Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.75,0:19:21.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, take this card.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.79,0:19:24.15,Default,,0,0,0,,The tie's a friendship.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.75,0:19:26.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I'd like you to have it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.73,0:19:27.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.81,0:19:32.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Say, Solomon, it's been ages\Nsince you and I have dueled.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.27,0:19:35.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that a challenge I\Nhear, Arthur? Oh, wow!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.79,0:19:37.41,Default,,0,0,0,,This I gotta see, dueling grandpa's!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.49,0:19:38.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.40,0:19:40.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Moto, remember, you just\Ngot out of the hospital.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.15,0:19:44.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, but I could out-duel any of you young\NTurks, even if I was still in a coma.
